50 observations: PR AUC mean 0.4954  sd 0.0229  range [0.4384, 0.5353]
That sd is wider than a single split's, and it should be: more splits
sample more of the split-to-split variation rather than averaging it
away. It is still one dataset sliced many ways, not many datasets -
which is what the corrected t-test exists to keep honest.

